# GNOME Extension JS

## Imports

Use ESM (`import`) — no `imports.*`. Shell resources:

```js
import * as Main from 'resource:///org/gnome/shell/ui/main.js';
import {Extension} from 'resource:///org/gnome/shell/extensions/extension.js';
```

## Notifications

```js
// ✅ Works
Main.notify('Cisco VPN', 'VPN connected');

// ❌ Broke notifications in production
new MessageTray.Source(...)
```

## Subprocess

Use `commandRunner.js` (`runner.sudo`, `runner.run`). openconnect flags in `vpnManager._buildCommand()`.

## State sync

Two layers: `stateMachine` (UI state) and `network.connected()` (reality). Extension monitor in `_updateStatus()` reconciles every 2s.

## Scope discipline

Match existing style: minimal diff, no over-abstraction, reuse managers from `bootstrap.js`.
